Spec: row and card hover affordance

Behavior

Hovering anywhere on a table row tints the entire row and changes the cursor to a pointer.
Clicking anywhere on the row navigates to that row's detail page. There is no separate "Browse" button.
Keyboard focus produces the same tint, so tabbing through rows looks identical to hovering.
The currently-selected row keeps a persistent tint plus a left border, distinct from hover.
Do not combine this with zebra striping — alternating backgrounds fight the hover tint and make it unreadable.

Markup pattern (stretched link)

Put a real <a> in the first cell and stretch its hit area over the row with a pseudo-element. This keeps the row a genuine link: keyboard-focusable, middle-clickable, right-click "copy link address" works, and screen readers announce it correctly. Do not put a click handler on the <tr> — that gives the hover appearance without any of the behavior.

html
<tr class="group relative cursor-pointer transition-colors duration-100
           hover:bg-emerald-50 focus-within:bg-emerald-50">
  <td class="px-3 py-2 font-medium">
    <a href="/tables/dbo/HASH_REGISTRY"
       class="after:absolute after:inset-0 after:content-['']
              focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-emerald-600 rounded">
      HASH_REGISTRY
    </a>
  </td>
  <td class="px-3 py-2 text-slate-500">dbo</td>
  <td class="px-3 py-2 text-right tabular-nums">6</td>
</tr>

The <tr> needs relative; the <a>'s after:absolute after:inset-0 then covers the full row.

Tokens

Hover / focus tint: emerald-50 (
#ecfdf5). Light enough that black text stays at full contrast.
Selected row: bg-emerald-50 + border-l-2 border-emerald-600.
Transition: transition-colors duration-100. Colour only — never transition transform or box-shadow on table rows, it causes jitter on fast pointer movement across many rows.
Row separator: border-b border-slate-100, so the tint reads as a continuous band.

Reports cards (same idea, different treatment)

Cards sit on the page background, so a fill tint looks muddy. Change the border and elevation instead:

html
<a href="/reports/asset"
   class="block rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4
          transition-[border-color,box-shadow] duration-150
          hover:border-emerald-600 hover:shadow-md
          focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-emerald-600">

The card is an <a> element itself, so no stretched-link trick is needed.

Accessibility floor

focus-visible:ring-2 on every interactive element — keyboard users must see focus.
Respect reduced motion: @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { * { transition: none } }.
Hover state must never be the only signal — the pointer cursor and the underlying link carry the meaning if hover is unavailable (touch).

If a row needs both navigation and an inline action (e.g. a Delete button), give the action class="relative z-10" so it sits above the stretched link and doesn't trigger navigation.
